# TASK: Rename the Entire Game Project to AETHWYRD

I have officially chosen **AETHWYRD** as the new name of my game and its world.

Your task is to perform a comprehensive, repository-wide name migration, replacing the previous name(s) with **AETHWYRD** wherever appropriate.

This is a naming migration, NOT a lore rewrite or a game redesign.

## 1. Naming conventions

Use these conventions consistently:

- Official world name: Aethwyrd
- Official game title: AETHWYRD
- Capitalized title in branding, logos and title screens: AETHWYRD
- Normal prose: Aethwyrd
- Adjectival form: Aethwyrdian (where grammatically appropriate)

Previous names that must be identified:
- Aetheria
- Aetherian
- Aetheria's
- Aetherias
- Aertheria
- Aertherian
- Any other clear spelling or grammatical variations of the old world name.

Replace these with the appropriate Aethwyrd equivalent.

Do not replace unrelated words merely because they contain similar letter sequences.

## 2. Repository-wide audit

Before modifying anything:

1. Inspect the entire repository structure.
2. Read the root Canon.md and all relevant documentation.
3. Identify every occurrence of the previous name.
4. Search source code, Markdown, JSON, YAML, XML, configuration files, localization files, assets, UI text, comments and metadata.
5. Identify references in file paths, folder names, identifiers, class names, namespaces, constants and resource keys.
6. Identify references in GitHub workflows, build scripts and project configuration.

Create a migration report listing:
- Files containing old names.
- Occurrences found.
- Files and folders requiring renaming.
- Potentially risky replacements.
- References that cannot safely be changed automatically.

